# Healthcare App — Agent Conventions

## Stack

- Expo SDK 57 + React Native + TypeScript (strict)
- Expo Router file-based navigation under `app/`
- `expo-print` for PDF generation
- `expo-sqlite` for local persistence
- Prefer pure functions for legal/template logic so they are Jest-testable without native modules

## Paths

- `types/` — shared domain types (no React imports)
- `services/` — side-effectful and pure domain services
- `data/` — static templates (health authorities, legal copy, patient vault)
- `app/patient/[id]/foiWizard.tsx` — FOI wizard UI
- `app/patient/[id]/foiStatus.tsx` — vault-backed FOI request status list
- `app/patient/[id]/call811Prep.tsx` — 811 caregiver script prep UI
- `app/patient/[id]/sbarExport.tsx` — 1-page SBAR export UI
- `app/digest/daily.tsx` / `app/digest/weekly.tsx` — caregiver digest dashboards (live FOI / labs / med marks)
- `hooks/useDigestNotificationRouting.ts` — notification tap → digest deep-links
- `app/patient/[id]/uploadDoc.tsx` — OCR capture + verification UI
- `app/patient/[id]/voiceDebrief.tsx` — post-visit voice debrief UI
- `app/sandbox/aiTest.tsx` — local Ollama / SaMD sandbox UI
- `app/sandbox/index.tsx` — QA core-loop sandbox (digest / SBAR / FOI / 811)
- `utils/mockSeeder.ts` — SQLite dummy Dad/Child profile seeder
- `app/patient/[id]/emergencyPass.tsx` — emergency QR + wallet card
- `app/patient/[id]/proxyAccess.tsx` — proxy roles, access log, age-out hand-off
- `app/patient/[id]/insights.tsx` — biomarker trends / visit-prep Insights
- `data/skInterop.ts` — MySask export playbook + SMART readiness (honest NOT_PUBLIC)
- `services/interop/skConnector.ts` — Saskatchewan FILE_IMPORT connector (FHIR JSON + MySask lab text)
- `app/patient/[id]/portalSync.tsx` — SK connector exercise surface (sample sync + JSON file import)
- `app/patient/[id]/askVault.tsx` — SaMD-safe ask-my-vault over MedicalEvents
- `services/interop/` — FHIR mapper + connector boundary (read/import only)
- `types/interop.ts` — SMART/FHIR import + HealthAuthorityInterop metadata
- `types/db.ts` — SQLite row/schema types (`MedicalEvents` + provenance)
- `db/` — SQLite schema + repository helpers

## Digital front door / interop rules

1. Clinical source of truth = health authority / provincial portal; local vault is the patient-owned copy that powers SBAR, digests, and 811.
2. Phase B connectors are **read/import only** — never write back to custodian systems.
3. Persist provenance on MedicalEvents: `sourceType`, `sourceAuthorityId`, `externalId`, `lastSyncedAt`.
4. Prefer automatic FHIR/CCD import when `HealthAuthorityContact.interop.syncMode` is `SMART_FHIR` or `FILE_IMPORT`; FOI remains the fallback for `MANUAL_ONLY` or failed sync.
5. `PORTAL_SCREENSHOT` kind must be inferred for portal chrome OCR; structured labs still fold into digest/SBAR/Insights.
6. Lab parsers attach stable internal codes + optional LOINC aliases via `services/labCodes.ts`.
7. Ask-my-vault / educational restatements always use `SAMD_SYSTEM_PROMPT` posture — cite MedicalEvent ids; never diagnose or prescribe.
8. Saskatchewan (`sk-sha` / MySask): public path is PDF/lab **FILE_IMPORT** (`importSkMySaskLabText`, `importSkFhirJsonExport`); do not claim a live SMART OAuth endpoint — see `SK_SMART_READINESS` in `data/skInterop.ts`.
9. Alberta (`ab-ahs` / MyHealth Records): same FILE_IMPORT pattern (`importAbMyHealthLabText`, `importAbFhirJsonExport`); see `data/abInterop.ts`. Shared helpers live in `services/interop/connector.ts`.
10. British Columbia (`bc-health-gateway`): Health Gateway Download records FILE_IMPORT (`importBcHealthGatewayLabText`, `importBcFhirJsonExport`); FOI for charts still uses Fraser/VCH/Island templates.
11. Ontario (`on-patient-portals`): fragmented MyChart/OLIS FILE_IMPORT (`importOnMyChartLabText`, `importOnFhirJsonExport`); FOI via UHN/Sunnybrook/OH under PHIPA. Do not invent a unified provincial SMART endpoint.
12. Québec (`qc-carnet-sante`): Carnet santé Québec FILE_IMPORT (`importQcCarnetLabText`, `importQcFhirJsonExport`); FOI via treating CIUSSS / Santé Québec.
13. Manitoba (`mb-shared`): eChart is clinician-facing — FILE_IMPORT via care-org portal OCR or eChart PHI lab copy (`importMbEchartLabText`, `importMbFhirJsonExport`); FOI via Shared Health / WRHA under PHIA. Do not invent a patient SMART endpoint.
14. Nova Scotia (`ns-nsha` / YourHealthNS): FILE_IMPORT (`importNsYourHealthLabText`, `importNsFhirJsonExport`); FOI via Nova Scotia Health. Do not claim a public SMART launch.
15. Remaining Canada (`data/canadaRemainingInterop.ts` + `canadaRemainingConnectors.ts`): NB MyHealthNB (`nb-myhealth`), NL MyHealthNL (`nl-nlhs`), PE MyHealthPEI (`pe-healthpei`), YT/NT/NU ATIPP-first FILE_IMPORT (`yt-hss`, `nt-nthssa`, `nu-health`). Territories have no general consumer portals — do not invent SMART endpoints. Shared kit: `fileImportProvinceKit.ts`.



## Proxy access rules

1. Roles: `PRIMARY_POA`, `SIBLING_COORDINATOR`, `EMERGENCY_PASS` with fixed permission sets from `ROLE_PERMISSIONS`.
2. Access log is append-only — revoke/age-out must never delete prior entries. Persist via `db/proxyAccess` (`ProxyGrants` + `ProxyAccessLog`).
3. `EMERGENCY_PASS` grants require `expiresAt`; expired grants deny checks.
4. Age-out hand-off marks parental `PRIMARY_POA` grants `AGED_OUT` at consent age (default 16); demo may force for younger profiles.
5. Wire Emergency Pass CTA to existing `emergencyPass` screen rather than reimplementing QR crypto.
6. Engine APIs that mutate or list grants/log are async.

## SBAR summarizer rules

1. `compileSBAR` is an Educational Context Summarizer only — never diagnose or prescribe.
2. Assessment = caregiver observations/concerns; Recommendation = questions + documents to bring.
3. Reuse `formatActiveMedications` from the 811 engine; tolerate nullish dose/frequency.
4. Resolve optional `appointmentId` via `getHousehold` / household schedules — do not invent a parallel appointment fixture.
5. `compileSBAR` is async: load CONFIRMED/PENDING_REVIEW MedicalEvents (or inject `options.medicalEvents` in tests); fold VISIT_DEBRIEF → Assessment and OCR labs/Rx → Background with SaMD-safe wording.
6. `generateSBARPDF` returns an `expo-print` URI (or base64 fallback); no separate SBAR SQLite table — MedicalEvents are the persistence source.
7. Always attach `SBAR_REGULATORY_NOTICE` to engine output and UI; surface `sourceEventSummaries` in the export preview.

## QA sandbox rules

1. `seedLocalSandboxData()` must create Dad (78) CKD/T2DM + 4 meds + SHA lab mock + visit debrief MedicalEvent and Child (4) SK vaccines.
2. Sandbox actions exercise real services (digest daily/weekly, FOI, 811, SBAR via `compileSBAR`/`generateSBARPDF`, emergency pass, OCR parse+save, voice debrief extract+save, SK connector sample sync) — no parallel hardcoded SBAR HTML path.
3. Digest triggers must surface the push alert payload for verification (daily + weekly).
4. Keep seed fixtures unit-testable without SQLite where possible (`getDadSandboxMedicalEvents`).
5. OCR/voice sandbox runners may skip Tesseract/mic via text overrides but must use the same parsers and MedicalEvents persistence.

## Emergency pass rules

1. Encrypt critical emergency context with AES-256-GCM; tokens are short-lived (default 4h).
2. QR encodes ciphertext only; wallet card PDF also prints human-readable alerts for offline ER use.
3. Override demo key via `EXPO_PUBLIC_EMERGENCY_PASS_KEY` in real deployments.
4. Never log decrypted emergency payloads.
5. Profiles live in `data/emergencyProfiles.ts` (include sandbox Child `pt-leo-04`); sandbox runner: `runDadEmergencyPassSandbox`.

## Local LLM bridge rules

1. Default Ollama endpoints: `http://localhost:11434` and Android `http://10.0.2.2:11434`.
2. Always send `SAMD_SYSTEM_PROMPT` — educational summarizer only; never diagnose/prescribe.
3. Support `llama3.2:3b` and `phi3:mini` (and other Ollama tags via config).
4. Offline simulator fallback must remain SaMD-safe when Ollama is unreachable.

## Voice debrief rules

1. Record with `expo-av`; prefer local Whisper mock (`127.0.0.1:8765`) over cloud STT.
2. Extraction is a summarizer only — no diagnosis or prescribing.
3. Persist as `MedicalEvents.kind = 'VISIT_DEBRIEF'` with `parsed.eventType = 'VISIT_DEBRIEF'`.
4. Caregiver must review/edit action items before `CONFIRMED`.

## OCR ingestion rules

1. Prefer on-device OCR (`tesseract.js`); never send document images to a remote OCR API.
2. Keep regex parsers (`parseLabResults`, `parsePrescription`) pure and unit-tested without Tesseract.
3. Save both `rawText` and `parsedJson` into `MedicalEvents`; initial OCR save is `PENDING_REVIEW`, confirm flow sets `CONFIRMED`.
4. Verification UI must let caregivers edit extracted fields before confirm.
5. Infer `PORTAL_SCREENSHOT` when portal chrome is detected (`inferMedicalEventKind`); portal events with labs clear `MISSING_LAB_UPLOAD` and feed SBAR Background.

## Digest / notification rules

1. `compileDailyDigest` / `compileWeeklyDigest` scan Aging Parent + Child + Self household profiles.
2. Daily scan includes meds today, appointments ≤72h with prep alerts, FOI pending >30 days, missing labs.
3. Prefer vault truth: live `FOIRequests` DRAFT age, MedicalEvents lab uploads, and `MedDoseMarks` via injectable `DigestDataLoaders` / `createLiveDigestLoaders()`. Fixture overdue tasks are fallbacks when FOI store is empty.
4. “Review FOI Status” opens `foiStatus` (list of saved requests), not a blank wizard.
5. Notifications: daily 07:00 and Sunday 16:00 via `expo-notifications`; deep-link to `/digest/daily` or `/digest/weekly`.
6. Root layout must subscribe to notification taps / cold-start via `subscribeDigestNotificationRouting` (`hooks/useDigestNotificationRouting.ts`).
7. Keep digest compilation testable with injectable `now` + loaders; mock `expo-notifications` in unit tests.

## 811 Call Assistant rules

1. `generate811Script` is a Contextual Summarizer / Caregiver Script Assistant only.
2. Never emit diagnostic verdicts, acuity scores, or treatment/prescription instructions.
3. Tolerate null/missing medication dose and frequency without crashing.
4. Frame output for answering the 811 nurse’s dispatcher script (they ask; caregiver answers from vault).
5. Always return `spokenIntroScript`, exactly 4 `dispatcherCueSheet` cues, `historicalRedFlags`, and exactly 3 `questionsToAskNurse`.
6. Call action uses `expo-linking` with `tel:811` only after a script is generated.

## FOI module rules

1. Always source facility addresses from `data/healthAuthorities.ts` templates — every Canadian province and territory must have ≥1 facility.
2. Legal declaration text must invoke the act for the selected jurisdiction (PHIPA / HIPA / HIA / FIPPA-PIPA / PHIA / PHIPAA / LSSSS-AIPDP / HIPMA-ATIPP / ATIPP / HIA-FOIPP as applicable). Catalog: `data/foiJurisdictions.ts`.
3. `generateFOIPDF` returns a print URI or base64 string from `expo-print`.
4. Persist via `FOIRequests` with status `DRAFT` or `DISPATCHED` only.
5. Do not log raw PHN/HIN values.
6. Keep wizard steps explicit; do not collapse Step 3 (authority proof) into Step 2.
7. `CanadianJurisdiction` is all 13 subdivision codes: AB BC MB NB NL NS NT NU ON PE QC SK YT.

## Testing

- Unit-test HTML/legal template builders without mocking Expo when possible.
- Smoke-test wizard wiring with lightweight Jest + mocks for `expo-print` / SQLite.

## Commits

- Feature work on `cursor/<name>-a310` branches.
- Prefer small, descriptive commits focused on the active slice.
